--- Variables ---

-- There aliases to name types or make custom types
Alias number=i32 to int.

-- Math expressions wrapped in a _<expr>_; And by default number is 32bit float
There is an "Expression" of kind number that is _42 * (sin(pi/2) - 3)_.
Say the meaning of "Expression".  -- Prints "-84.0"

-- Constant cannot be changed later.
There is a constant "Constant" of kind int that is 42.
-( same as say, but explicidly states output to 'me' (stdout here),
   and doesnt include newline by default )-
Tell me the meaning of "Constant"
Say nothing.  -- Just prints newline, nothing or nil is like None in pyhton

-- "There is" and "there was" both are keywords to define a variable
Once there was a "Boolean" of kind boolean that is true.

-- Text in `` is treated like text (string variable) no matter what's inside
There was a "String" of kind text that is `true`.
-- "... of kind text that is true." --- implicit cast boolean to string

Then "Expression" became _$"Constant" + 27_.
Tell me `Expression = $"Expression".\n`  -- Prints "69.0"

Then "Expression" became _$"Expression" + 1.11e1_.  -- 80.1
Say the meaning as int of "Expression".  -- Prints "80"
-- Alternative: Say _int($"Expression")_.  --- Also prints "80"
